<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ terms of trade rose 0.2 pct in Sept qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ terms of trade rose 0.2 pct in Sept qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand (SNZ) on Wednesday released the following provisional overseas trade, price, volume and terms of trade indices for the September 1996 quarter.</p>
<p>			     (percentage)</p>
<p>				 Sept 1996   June 1996    Sept 1995</p>
<p>Terms of Trade		 +0.2	   -0.7	  -0.8</p>
<p>Export Price Index	   -0.8	   -2.1	  +0.9</p>
<p>Import price Index	   -0.9	   -1.1	  +1.7</p>
<p>Import price changes (percentage) from previous qtr</p>
<p>					  Sept quarter  June quarter</p>
<p>    Food and beverages		  +0.4		+3.9</p>
<p>    Petroleum and products	    +2.9		-3.3</p>
<p>    Non-fuel crude materials	  -4.4		-1.2</p>
<p>    Plastics, plastic articles	-1.3		-0.8</p>
<p>    Textile yarn, fabric		+5.1		-5.0</p>
<p>    Iron and steel			-2.4		-1.6</p>
<p>    Non-electrical machinery	   --		 +1.1</p>
<p>    Electrical machinery		-5.7		+0.4</p>
<p>    Transport equipment		 +1.1		-2.6</p>
<p>		Main export price changes  (percentage)</p>
<p>					  Sept quarter   June quarter</p>
<p>    Dairy products			-1.9		-8.6</p>
<p>    Meat, wool, byproducts	    +3.9		+0.2</p>
<p>    Fish, fish preparations	   -2.7		+2.6</p>
<p>    Food and beverages		  -0.7		-1.2</p>
<p>    Forestry products		   -2.0		-8.8</p>
<p>    Non-fuel crude materials	  -0.2		-5.8</p>
<p>    Aluminium			     -6.0		-1.6</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
